{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792777059,"nonce":"d909zJXZi7Zv5GbzD9/vC2OdoCg=","title":"Python: a drained generator stays reachable since one string-literal global per text","message":"`crates/zyntax_python/pressure/generators.py` (a generator started, drained and dropped every step) grows with the step count, and `memory_pressure::peak_memory_does_not_grow_with_the_step_count` fails: \"generators.py: peak memory grew from 35 MB to 156 MB between 2000 and 400000 steps, about 193 bytes a step\" (Mac, release, llvm-backend).\n\nWith `ZYNTAX_TRACE_GC=1` the collector's reached set grows with the steps (3.5, 7.0, 13.8 MB at collections 5 to 7 for 100000 steps), so the generators are still referenced, not missed by the sweep.\n\nBisected on the NUC (generators.py peak RSS at 2000 vs 400000 steps, ZYNTAX_GC_FLOOR_KB=512 ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1): cd5306b8 64 MB flat, 45e070db flat, 701ca7cd 55 to 244 MB. First bad commit 701ca7cd \"Lowering: one string-literal global per text in a module\". The drained generator's `zb_fiber_free` is still emitted in `main`.","files":null}]}